  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>Mt. San Antonio College is a public community college in Walnut, California. It was founded in 1945 and offers more than 400 degree and certificate programs, 36 support programs, and more than 50 student clubs &amp; athletic programs.</p><p>Mt. San Antonio College is a Top 10 California Transfer College that attracts vast numbers of international students annually to its courses.</p> <p>The college is a welcoming environment conducive to integrative learning. Students have easy access to the campus, access to a GoPass enabling free transportation via bus or rail and a scenic campus spanning 420 acres on the eastern edge of the Greater Los Angeles area. The plethora of multiple clubs, athletics opportunities, and student support services empower students to do more than just study.</p>  <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Athletics is a big part of student life in American colleges, and Mt. San Antonio College is no exception. The athletics teams have been nationally recognised, and regular game attendance is an excellent way to socialise with like-minded students. Over 60 student clubs are available for students to pursue their hobbies and interests, with the Student Leadership and Advisor Awards ceremony acting as a great motivator for students to become an active part of campus life. Volunteering is encouraged to foster a sense of belonging to the community in addition to earning students recognition. Students feel valued at Mt. San Antonio College.</p> "
    ],
